Judged and fine:
- The retry runs only when err == nil, so never after a timeout or a shutdown cancel (runOnce returns "aborted" in both cases).
- The retry's RunOnceContext refuses to start on a ctx that is already done, so a cancel that races an exiting npm cannot start a second npm.
- The retry shares ictx, so both installs fit in the one bridgeInstallTimeout.
- Both calls go through sup.RunOnceContext; internal/supervisor is unchanged.
- After a retry, the marker flow is the unchanged default branch, confirmed end to end.
- The output buffer keeps a 1 MiB head and tail, so npm's closing "npm error code" line survives a long output.
- TestMain calls m.Run unless the env var is set. It is the package's only TestMain, it sits in a test-only file, and t.Setenv keeps parallel tests out, so it cannot reach the shipped binary.

