Residual design risk, not a finding (for Getty):
- The "no error code" trigger also catches a code-less failure that has nothing to do with peers: npm killed from outside, an out-of-memory crash, another npm bug.
- The retry then installs a legacy-peer tree. Because the smoke test checks only initialize and the marker skips later installs, a tree that lacks a peer the bridge loads lazily can stay in place.
- The log line names the flag, and the README says what the flag leaves out.

